+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Prism Breaker release requirements</title><h1>Release acceptance contract</h1>
+<p>This is the adopted executable scope for handbook 2.8. Browser evidence is local Chromium with named CSS viewport fixtures. Physical Android/iOS, native share receipt, OS eviction, screen-reader speech and full WCAG conformance remain unverified. The existing device/human plan remains separate; these rows do not waive those outcomes or authorize broader claims.</p>
+<main id="requirements" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirements" data-version="1">
+<article id="storage" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="browser"><h2>Save failure and next action</h2><p>Checkpoint failure stays unconfirmed; failed leave keeps the working run; retry saves before leaving.</p></article>
+<article id="editor" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="browser"><h2>DOM authoring and durable drafts</h2><p>Current form values, stable node identity, no selection-only save, failed write recovery, transactional stale-revision refusal, preview isolation and inert import.</p></article>
+<article id="layout" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="browser"><h2>Sampled interface accessibility</h2><p>Help/settings/leaderboard/results at 320×640, 390×844, 844×390 and 1100×800, dark/light themes, double text sizes, no dialog horizontal overflow, named dialogs, sampled opaque-heading contrast and reachable focused controls. This does not certify all criteria or simulate an OS keyboard.</p></article>
+<article id="performance" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="browser"><h2>Controlled comparison and sustained rendering</h2><p>Four counterbalanced 300-frame quiet direct-render samples with the same drawing size and quality, plus 3600 active frames, finite timing, bounded particles and retained resource counts. The named desktop profile requires at least 40% fewer quiet draw submissions, sustained p95 intervals at most 25 ms, maximum at most 250 ms and p95 CPU submission at most 12 ms. Retain p95/p99/max and raw samples; no universal FPS or GPU-time claim.</p></article>
+<article id="contracts" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="suite"><h2>Executable recovery and input contracts</h2><meta itemprop="artifact" content="tests/handbook-recovery.test.mjs"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="tests/offline.test.mjs"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="tests/paddle-collision.test.mjs"><p>Pointer ownership/cancellation, canonical score reconciliation, jitter/backoff, transactional acknowledgement, late restore failure and next ordinary action pass in the full behavioral suite.</p></article>
+<article id="assets" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="artifact"><h2>Required deliverable inventory</h2><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/favicon.svg"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/favicon.ico"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/apple-touch-icon.png"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/assets/og-prism-breaker.jpg"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/assets/og-prism-breaker-square.jpg"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/assets/prism-maskable-512.png"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/assets/FONT-LICENSE.txt"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="public/vendor/THREE-LICENSE.txt"><p>These exports are required independently of the generated precache inventory.</p></article>
+<article id="operations" itemscope itemtype="urn:PrismBreaker:Requirement" data-kind="artifact"><h2>Trust, retention and recovery contract</h2><meta itemprop="artifact" content="PUBLIC-DATA-OPERATIONS.md"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="DOCUMENT-FIRST-ARCHITECTURE.md"><meta itemprop="artifact" content="RELEASE-PUBLICATION.md"><p>Owner DAV and casual scores remain selected. Native policies are preserved. Access-driven physical cleanup, local retention and bounded diagnostic/privacy/abuse response are explicit.</p></article>
+</main></html>
